  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">FTF Bangladesh Livestock and Nutrition Activity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Bangladesh):  The FTF Bangladesh Livestock and Nutrition activity aims to sustainably increase the productivity of livestock, as well as the marketability and consumption of livestock products. With FY 2024 funds, the activity will facilitate productivity-enhancing technologies and practices such as processing and preservation of fodder for year-round livestock feeding; support enhanced dairy processing and preservation into diversified nutritious products, especially in rural areas; promote the consumption of diversified and safe livestock products; and collaborate with appropriate agencies, such as the Department of Livestock Services, the Bangladesh Livestock Research Institute, and the Food and Agriculture Organization Emergency Center for Transboundary Diseases. The activity will facilitate access to credit, including microfinance. The activity will adopt a market systems approach and engage the private sector to ensure the sustainability of its interventions, contributing to improved food security in Bangladesh. The activity will promote climate-smart technologies and practices, such as saline and flood-tolerant fodder varieties along the coastal belt of the country. It will strengthen the capacity of artificial insemination technicians to provide services that will improve livestock breeds, which are able to withstand environmental shocks and stresses. The activity aligns with the three objectives of the U.S. government&apos;s Global Food Security Strategy. Funding  contributes to Adaptation - Indirect ($2.5m), Gender Equality and Women Empowerment Secondary ($735k), Microenterprises and Livelihoods ($200k); Private Sector Engagement ($1m); and Sustainable Landscapes - Indirect ($500k), Food Security R&amp;D (1,488,732) earmarks and key issues.</narrative>
  </description>
